As repeated frequently, ttyrecs do not provide accurate information as
to how many potions were generated and are not a suitable source of
info for this particular scenario.

Even if they did, they are not trivial to parse, as they must be sorted 
into individual games, then joined together, and then properly decoded 
to find not only things named "potion of healing", but determine exactly 
which potion _was_ the potion of healing and pick out all the un-IDed 
potions that the player found prior to IDing which was healing.

Contrast with the difficulty of simply writing a patch for NAO that
would intercept all object generation and log it (along with dlevel
generated) -- and that such a patch would provide 100% accurate
information, no bias possible.  If you are not familiar with how objects
are generated in Nethack, it is a simple task to hook these routines and
write the output to a file.

